it_twice.plain, line 2: Split this line into two steps, so "it" has only one meaning.

    ask "Pick one" with choices scores where it is more than 60 and call it pick
                                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try this:
    set matching scores to scores where it is more than 60
    ask "Pick one" with choices matching scores and call it pick
Why: Inside "where", "it" means each item being checked, but in "and call it" it means what the step gives back. One word can't mean two things in one line.

